Package: lightbox
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, iptables | nftables
Suggests: squid
Description: minimal, secure container runtime in one static binary
 lightbox turns a directory that holds a Linux root filesystem into
 containers: namespaces, cgroup v2 limits, an address on a bridge of the
 host's, and a sandbox that is on unless an option turns it off. It has no
 daemon and is linked without a C library.
 .
 A profile for boxes that hold an AI agent's working session adds a user
 namespace, an allow-list seccomp filter, no network or a proxy alone, time
 limits, and an audit log of every command.
